---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { company } from '../config';
import { handover } from '../data';
---
<Base title="About" description={`${company.name} is a BMS controls company in ${company.location}. Your site, your system, your keys: every login, file and licence is handed over.`}>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Your site. Your system. Your keys.</h1>
      <p class="lead">We build it, you own it.</p>

      <div class="todo">
        <p>
          <!-- TODO(Dan): rewrite in your own words. Keep it honest and specific. -->
          {company.name} is a BMS controls company based in {company.location}. The engineer who
          writes the software is the one on site commissioning it, so nothing is lost between design and handover.
        </p>
        <p>
          [Your background: years in controls, the platforms you've worked on, the kinds of
          buildings, and why you set up {company.name}.]
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Why we hand everything over</h2>
      <p>
        In building controls it's common for the installer to keep the admin passwords, the controller
        programs and the software licences. The building owner can't change a time schedule, add a point
        or bring in another engineer without going back to them. The system was paid for, but it isn't
        really theirs.
      </p>
      <p>
        We work the other way. When a job is finished, everything needed to run, maintain and change the
        system is handed to you. If you want us to look after it, we'd be glad to. If you'd rather use
        someone else, they'll have everything they need.
      </p>

      <h2>What you get at handover</h2>
      <ul>
        {handover.map((h) => <li><strong>{h.title}.</strong> {h.summary}</li>)}
      </ul>

      <h2>How we work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>One point of contact from strategy through to handover</li>
        <li>Clear documentation: strategies, point schedules, drawings and O&amp;M information</li>
        <li>Flexible: full packages or individual parts for building owners, M&amp;E and controls contractors</li>
      </ul>

      <!-- TODO(Dan): accreditations, insurance, CSCS/ECS cards, H&S schemes (e.g. CHAS, SafeContractor) if held -->
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
